{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.WLambdaMTCLocalizationObligation","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.WLambdaMTCLocalizationObligation","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.Finset.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneC2QDimTranspose"],"declarations":20,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.heckeLocalizationOfPos_full_support","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.heckeLocalizationOfPos_full_support","kind":"theorem","line":257,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/WLambdaMTCLocalizationObligation.lean#L257-L268","doc":"**C6 strengthened — the support is *all* of `P`.** The set of blocks with nonzero Plancherel\nweight is exactly the full block set: no block is dropped (`full support`, the no-finite-`N`-Sasakian\nnecessary condition). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.heckeLocalizationOfPos_loc_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.heckeLocalizationOfPos_loc_pos","kind":"theorem","line":246,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/WLambdaMTCLocalizationObligation.lean#L246-L255","doc":"**C6 — full support (derived).** For `q > 1` every block of the real Hecke localization carries\nstrictly positive Plancherel weight: `loc p = d_q(p)²/D² > 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.heckeLocalizationOfPos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.heckeLocalizationOfPos","kind":"def","line":228,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/WLambdaMTCLocalizationObligation.lean#L228-L236","doc":"**`heckeLocalization` with `D² ≠ 0` discharged from positivity** (`q > 1`, `P` nonempty) —\nthe last structural input is now *derived*, not assumed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.sum_qDimSq_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.sum_qDimSq_pos","kind":"theorem","line":221,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/WLambdaMTCLocalizationObligation.lean#L221-L226","doc":"**`D² = Σ_λ d_q(λ)² > 0`** on a nonempty block set for `q > 1` — so `globalDim_ne` holds\ndirectly from positivity, **without** the (false) `Σ d_q² = [n]_q!` identity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.qDim_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.qDim_pos","kind":"theorem","line":209,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/WLambdaMTCLocalizationObligation.lean#L209-L219","doc":"**`d_q(λ) > 0` for `q > 1`** — the genuine Hecke q-dimension is positive in the substrate\nregime. Numerator `[n]_q! > 0` (`qFactorial_pos`); the denominator is a product of\n`qBracket q h > 0` over genuine cells (`qBracket_pos`, hooks `≥ 1`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.heckeLocalization","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.heckeLocalization","kind":"def","line":147,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/WLambdaMTCLocalizationObligation.lean#L147-L179","doc":"**Real Hecke q-Plancherel wire-up (removes the abstract `qDim_conj`).**\n\nBuilds a `BeasleyWittenLocalization ℝ` from the **genuine** Hecke q-dimension\n`qDim` ([`QPartitionCombinatorics.qDim`](../MathlibExt/QPartitionCombinatorics.lean),\n`d_q(λ) = [n]_q! / ∏_c [h_c]_q`) on any conjugate-closed set of sorted partitions `P` with\n`D² = Σ_λ d_q(λ)² ≠ 0`. The `loc` IS the categorical Plancherel measure `d_q²/D²` (so `loc_matches`\nis `rfl`), and — the point of the strengthening — the `qDim_conj` field is discharged by the\n**corpus-proved** `QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.qDim_conj`\n([`KeystoneC2QDimTranspose.lean`](KeystoneC2QDimTranspose.lean), sorry-free), **not** carried\nabstractly. So `loc_isProbabilityMeasure` (C1) and `loc_conj_eq` (C2) hold for the *actual* Hecke\nPlancherel measure of the blocks `P`, modulo only the structural inputs (conj-closure, `D² ≠ 0`).\n\n`D² ≠ 0` is the sole remaining hypothesis. It does **not** depend on any Wedderburn sum identity:\n`D² = Σ_λ d_q²` is its own q-polynomial and is **not** `[n]_q!` (the claim\n`Σ d_q² = [n]_q!` is false at generic q — see\n[`docs/audits/2026-06-29-wedderburn-trace-identity-false-at-generic-q.md`](../../../../../docs/audits/2026-06-29-wedderburn-trace-identity-false-at-generic-q.md)).\nFor `1 < q` it is discharged directly from positivity (`qBracket_pos`/`qFactorial_pos` ⇒\n`d_q > 0` ⇒ `Σ d_q² > 0`) — a clean follow-up; carried as a hypothesis here. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.Example.localization_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.Example.localization_two","kind":"instance","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/WLambdaMTCLocalizationObligation.lean#L119-L139","doc":"**Non-vacuity witness — `BeasleyWittenLocalization ℚ` is inhabited (`n = 2`).** The partitions\nof `2` are `[2]` (trivial) and `[1,1]` (sign), both of q-dimension `d_q = 1` at any `q` (the\none-cell hook products cancel), so `D² = 2`, the Plancherel measure is `loc ≡ 1/2`, and transpose\nswaps the two blocks. Both class fields check by `decide` / `norm_num`. This confirms the\nconditional theorems above are **not** conditional-on-`False`: there is a genuine model where the\nmatching holds against the actual `n=2` block combinatorics. (Stronger `n=4` and `n=5` witnesses\nwith the genuine non-trivial `d_q` values — the physical electron/muon blocks — are supplied in\n[`KeystoneWLambdaPhysicalBlocks.lean`](KeystoneWLambdaPhysicalBlocks.lean).) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.loc_conj_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.loc_conj_eq","kind":"theorem","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/WLambdaMTCLocalizationObligation.lean#L108-L113","doc":"**C2 — chirality-blindness (derived).** Any localization matching `d_q²/D²` is\ntranspose-invariant: `loc λ′ = loc λ`. Transports the corpus-proved `qDim_conj`\n(`d_q(λ′)=d_q(λ)`) onto `loc` via the matching. The keystone necessary condition C2 for the\ngauge-theory weight — derived, not assumed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.loc_isProbabilityMeasure","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.loc_isProbabilityMeasure","kind":"theorem","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/WLambdaMTCLocalizationObligation.lean#L99-L106","doc":"**C1 — normalization (derived).** Any localization matching `d_q²/D²` is a probability measure:\n`Σ_λ loc λ = 1`. The `D²` cancels by construction (`Finset.sum_div` + `div_self globalDim_ne`).\nThis is the keystone's C1 normalization — the genuine Plancherel `D² = Σ d_q²` normaliser forces\n`Σ = 1` (unlike `[n]_q!`). Derived from `loc_matches`, not assumed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.BeasleyWittenLocalization.loc_matches","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.BeasleyWittenLocalization.loc_matches","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/WLambdaMTCLocalizationObligation.lean#L95-L95","doc":"**THE MTC-MATCHING OBLIGATION (residual i).** The localization equals our category's\nPlancherel measure `d_q(λ)² / D²`. The single unproved field — what the owner-gated gauge datum\nmust deliver. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.BeasleyWittenLocalization.loc","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.BeasleyWittenLocalization.loc","kind":"def","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/WLambdaMTCLocalizationObligation.lean#L91-L91","doc":"The Beasley–Witten / RT localization weight on the blocks (the gauge-theory side). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.BeasleyWittenLocalization.globalDim_ne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.BeasleyWittenLocalization.globalDim_ne","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/WLambdaMTCLocalizationObligation.lean#L89-L89","doc":"The global quantum dimension `D² = Σ_λ d_q(λ)²` is nonzero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.BeasleyWittenLocalization.qDim_conj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.BeasleyWittenLocalization.qDim_conj","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/WLambdaMTCLocalizationObligation.lean#L87-L87","doc":"**Corpus-proved input** `d_q(λ′) = d_q(λ)` (`KeystoneC2QDimTranspose.qDim_conj`,\nsorry-free) — carried abstractly here (Mathlib-only module). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.BeasleyWittenLocalization.qDim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.BeasleyWittenLocalization.qDim","kind":"def","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/WLambdaMTCLocalizationObligation.lean#L84-L84","doc":"The categorical q-dimension `d_q(λ)` of the Hecke block. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.BeasleyWittenLocalization.conj_mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.BeasleyWittenLocalization.conj_mem","kind":"theorem","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/WLambdaMTCLocalizationObligation.lean#L82-L82","doc":"The blocks are closed under transpose (`λ ⊢ n ⇒ λ′ ⊢ n`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.BeasleyWittenLocalization.conj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.BeasleyWittenLocalization.conj","kind":"def","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/WLambdaMTCLocalizationObligation.lean#L80-L80","doc":"The transpose involution `λ ↦ λ′`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.BeasleyWittenLocalization.parts","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.BeasleyWittenLocalization.parts","kind":"def","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/WLambdaMTCLocalizationObligation.lean#L78-L78","doc":"The finite set of Hecke partition blocks `λ ⊢ n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.BeasleyWittenLocalization.Part","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.BeasleyWittenLocalization.Part","kind":"def","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/WLambdaMTCLocalizationObligation.lean#L76-L76","doc":"Partition index for `λ ⊢ n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.BeasleyWittenLocalization.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.BeasleyWittenLocalization.mk","kind":"ctor","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/WLambdaMTCLocalizationObligation.lean#L74-L74","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.BeasleyWittenLocalization","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.BeasleyWittenLocalization","kind":"class","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/WLambdaMTCLocalizationObligation.lean#L63-L95","doc":"**Residual (i): the Beasley–Witten / RT localization, matched to the Hecke Plancherel measure.**\n\nCarries the Hecke partition blocks `parts` for `λ ⊢ n`, the transpose involution `conj`\n(`λ ↦ λ′`), the categorical q-dimension `qDim = d_q`, and — as its single unproved field — the\n**MTC-matching obligation** `loc_matches`: the gauge-theory localization weight `loc` equals the\ncategorical Plancherel measure `d_q(λ)² / D²`, `D² = Σ_λ d_q(λ)²`. This is exactly what the\nowner-gated gauge datum on `S³/2I` must deliver; it is **not** constructed here.\n\nThe two structural inputs `conj_mem` (blocks closed under transpose) and `qDim_conj` (the\ncorpus-proved `d_q(λ′) = d_q(λ)`) are established facts, not the conclusions; `globalDim_ne` is\n`D² ≠ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}